  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own 'Financial Summary' multi-year summary table (audited), Solo/Standalone basis. Reporting basis confirmed by matching this dataset's recorded Total Assets against the bank's own separate (Solo) Balance Sheet, which is consistently lower than its Consolidated Balance Sheet (the bank consolidates an Offshore Banking Unit and a brokerage subsidiary, SJIBL Securities Limited) -- directly verified in FY2013, FY2014, FY2020, FY2022 and FY2025 (see sources.json). As a Shariah-based Islamic bank, Shahjalal Islami Bank PLC reports 'Investment' rather than conventional 'Loans and Advances', and 'Classified Investment'/'Non-Performing Investment' rather than 'NPL', consistent with the convention used elsewhere in this dataset for EXIMBANK and FIRSTSBANK. Total Liabilities is not a separate line in the summary table and is calculated as Total Assets minus Total Shareholders' Equity. RESTATEMENT FOUND: Total Assets for FY2013 is contemporaneously reported here as 121,963.43mn (matches the FY2013 report's own Solo Balance Sheet exactly, printed line 'Total Property and Assets', annual_reports line ~7238). The FY2014 annual report's own comparative Solo Balance Sheet for 31.12.2013 instead shows Total Property and Assets = 128,554.28mn (annual_reports line ~7219) -- a genuine restatement of +6,590.84mn (+5.40%), driven entirely by a symmetric gross-up of 'Other Assets' (4,564.45mn -> 11,155.29mn) and 'Other Liabilities' (6,093.07mn -> 12,683.91mn) by the identical amount (6,590.84mn) -- i.e. Total Liabilities also restates from 111,012.15mn to 117,602.99mn, preserving the balance-sheet identity in BOTH versions. Non-Profit Earning Assets in the summary table shows the same pattern (21,529 own -> 28,120 per FY2014+ reports). Both versions are internally consistent (assets=liabilities+equity holds in each), so this is a genuine restatement, not an arithmetic error -- the contemporaneous FY2013 figure (121,963.43 / 21,529) is kept per project rule, and this note documents the divergence. This is the largest restatement found in this bank's 15-year history.",
